  "details": "Users may get kicked or banned from an instance and have no reason, or ability to determine the reason. I still want to keep kicks fast, so I think it would be helpful to have a custom message set by the group that displays on the kick message screen some information about the kick (i.e. how to appeal a ban). It should also send a notification that they can look at later, i.e. to reference a Discord server link that they need to use to appeal.\n\nA slightly alternative approach would be that, once a person is kicked, the menu stays open and offers a group-defined reason list, each of which would come with a message sent as a notification to the kicked or banned user (and saved in the group audit logs to aid with any possible paperwork later) to tell them what rule they broke. This would replace the notification, but not the message on the kick/ban screen. If there are no instance kick reasons defined in a group, then, the in-game kick/ban flow would work exactly as it does now.\n\nIn any case, the end goal is that people know what they were kicked for and how to appeal, and users do not need to hunt for that information.",
